# layer 2: binary blocks (BW write, BR read, BU upload), optional CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE
GI
?
!reply 0 480 320 16 256 B4096
# 4x2 block, with LF (0A) bytes inside the data and the closing LF after it
BW 10 10 4 2
!bin 01 02 0A 04 05 06 07 08 0A
!err 0
!pixel 0 10 10 1
!pixel 0 12 10 10
!pixel 0 13 11 8
BR 10 10 4 2
!replyhex 01020A0405060708
BR 10 10 4 2 1
!replyhex 01020A04050607080F70
# with a CRC: a good one writes, a bad one writes nothing
BW 20 20 2 1 1
!bin 05 07 92 1D 0A
!err 0
!pixel 0 20 20 5
!pixel 0 21 20 7
BW 30 30 2 1 1
!bin 05 07 92 1E 0A
!err 12
!pixel 0 30 30 0
# limits and framing errors
BW 0 0 65 64
!err 13
BW 0 0 0 4
!err 4
BW 0 0 1 1 2
!err 4
BR 478 0 4 1
!err 5
BW 0 0 1 1:K 2
!err 2
# a missing LF after the block: SYNC, then skip to the next LF; later lines work
BW 40 40 1 1
!bin 05 41 42 0A
!err 14
!pixel 0 40 40 5
W 3 3 9
!err 0
!pixel 0 3 3 9
# upload an image as raw indices (all opaque), place it, read it back
BU 0 2 2
!bin 0B 0C 0D 0E 0A
!err 0
?I 0
!reply 2 2
IP 0 100 100
!pixel 0 100 100 11
!pixel 0 101 101 14
BT 12:IP 0 200 200:BT
!pixel 0 201 200 0
!pixel 0 200 200 11
BU 32 1 1
!err 4
